unzip: -% extracts an entry whose name is not UTF-8 under an escaped name (homescoop#1224).
Off by default: without -% such an entry is still refused (EILSEQ,
"cannot create", rc 50, homescoop#602). With -%, a name that is not
valid UTF-8 (the realm's strict decoder: no overlongs, surrogates or
code points past U+10FFFF) has each byte outside a valid sequence
written as %XX and each % as %25; a name that is valid UTF-8 is left
alone. An escaped entry is refused (rc 2) when its path exists already,
on disk or from this run, under -o and -n too, and a later entry whose
path an escaped entry took is refused the same way, so no mapped name
ever replaces a file. Each escaped path is reported ("escaped: <path>").

